      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "There are 5 ways to choose the odd digits for the units place.  There are 9 ways to choose each of the thousands and hundreds digits.  There is only 1 way to choose the tens digit that makes the number a four digit number.  Hence, $A = 5 \\times 9 \\times 9 \\times 1 = 360$.\n\nThere are 5 ways to choose the last digit and 10 ways to the first.  Hence, $B = 5 \\times 10 = 50$.  Thus, $A + B = 360 + 50 = 410$.  The answer is 410.",
